# Testing Standards

## Test Organization

Reference [src/__tests__/](mdc:src/__tests__/) for test structure:

- [comprehensive.test.ts](mdc:src/__tests__/comprehensive.test.ts) - Comprehensive validation tests
- [performance.test.ts](mdc:src/__tests__/performance.test.ts) - Performance optimization tests
- [coverage.test.ts](mdc:src/__tests__/coverage.test.ts) - Code coverage tests
- [index.test.ts](mdc:src/__tests__/index.test.ts) - Main API tests

## Test Configuration

Use [jest.config.js](mdc:jest.config.js) for test setup and [tsconfig.json](mdc:tsconfig.json) for TypeScript configuration.

## Case-Insensitive Testing

Test case-insensitive keyword handling:

```typescript
describe('Case-insensitive SQL keywords', () => {
  test('should accept lowercase keywords', () => {
    expect(isSnowflakeSQLValid('select * from table1')).toBe(true);
  });
  
  test('should accept uppercase keywords', () => {
    expect(isSnowflakeSQLValid('SELECT * FROM TABLE1')).toBe(true);
  });
  
  test('should reject mixed case keywords', () => {
    expect(isSnowflakeSQLValid('sElEcT * fRoM tAbLe1')).toBe(false);
  });
});
```

## Performance Testing

Test caching and optimization features:

```typescript
describe('Performance optimization', () => {
  test('should cache parser instances', () => {
    const startTime = Date.now();
    validateSnowflakeSQL('SELECT * FROM table1');
    const firstParse = Date.now() - startTime;
    
    const startTime2 = Date.now();
    validateSnowflakeSQL('SELECT * FROM table1');
    const secondParse = Date.now() - startTime2;
    
    expect(secondParse).toBeLessThan(firstParse);
  });
  
  test('should track performance statistics', () => {
    const stats = SnowflakeSQL.getPerformanceStats();
    expect(stats.totalParses).toBeGreaterThan(0);
    expect(stats.averageParseTime).toBeGreaterThan(0);
  });
});
```

## Error Handling Testing

Test error reporting and validation:

```typescript
describe('Error handling', () => {
  test('should report syntax errors with line/column info', () => {
    const result = validateSnowflakeSQL('SELECT * FROM');
    expect(result.isValid).toBe(false);
    expect(result.errors[0]).toHaveProperty('startLine');
    expect(result.errors[0]).toHaveProperty('startColumn');
    expect(result.errors[0]).toHaveProperty('message');
  });
  
  test('should provide helpful suggestions', () => {
    const result = validateSnowflakeSQL('SELECT * FROM');
    expect(result.errors[0]).toHaveProperty('suggestions');
    expect(Array.isArray(result.errors[0].suggestions)).toBe(true);
  });
});
```

## Cache Testing

Test caching behavior:

```typescript
describe('Caching behavior', () => {
  beforeEach(() => {
    SnowflakeSQL.clearCache();
  });
  
  test('should cache normalized SQL', () => {
    const stats1 = SnowflakeSQL.getCacheStats();
    validateSnowflakeSQL('SELECT * FROM table1');
    const stats2 = SnowflakeSQL.getCacheStats();
    expect(stats2.size).toBeGreaterThan(stats1.size);
  });
  
  test('should respect cache limits', () => {
    // Fill cache beyond limit
    for (let i = 0; i < 1100; i++) {
      validateSnowflakeSQL(`SELECT * FROM table${i}`);
    }
    const stats = SnowflakeSQL.getCacheStats();
    expect(stats.size).toBeLessThanOrEqual(stats.limit);
  });
});
```

## Integration Testing

Test complete validation workflow:

```typescript
describe('Integration tests', () => {
  test('should validate complex SQL with CTEs', () => {
    const complexSQL = `
      WITH cte1 AS (
        SELECT * FROM table1 WHERE column1 > 10
      )
      SELECT * FROM cte1 JOIN table2 ON cte1.id = table2.id
    `;
    const result = validateSnowflakeSQL(complexSQL);
    expect(result.isValid).toBe(true);
  });
  
  test('should handle React integration', () => {
    // Test that the library can be imported in React context
    const { validateSnowflakeSQL } = require('../index');
    expect(typeof validateSnowflakeSQL).toBe('function');
  });
});
```

## Test Best Practices

- Use descriptive test names that explain the expected behavior
- Test both positive and negative cases
- Include performance benchmarks for optimization features
- Test error boundaries and edge cases
- Verify caching behavior and memory management
- Test case-insensitive keyword handling thoroughly
- Include integration tests for complex SQL patterns
